<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goris is a town in the Syunik province of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. It is known for the cave dwellings of Old Goris and for its town of stone houses laid out on a regular plan in the 1870s. In 1921 it was the seat of the anti-Bolshevik Republic of Mountainous Armenia led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garegin-nzhdeh">Garegin Nzhdeh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goris.jpg" alt="Goris" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See above · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goris_new_mix_2021.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
